The baseline unfiltered run completed 426 tests but exited 1 because the existing dirty HEV test failed four assertions; the target LibSSH test passed but consumed 4.116 seconds—almost exactly two sequential remote `sleep 2` lifetimes. That confirms the cancellation test was coupling cleanup to wall-clock subprocess exit while its cleanup deadlines used a frozen manual clock. I’m replacing that fixture protocol with an EOF-driven `cat` round trip, retaining stronger same-channel and sibling usability checks, and making sshd shutdown reap the process before deleting its fixture directory.
